            <ArticleTitle>Isolated Congenital Left Ventricular Diverticulum: A Case Report and Differential Diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2211-4122.178467</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of an incidental finding of diverticulum in a patient presented to the Emergency Department for atypical chest pain, and we analyze the challenging differential diagnosis with aneurysm, pseudoaneurysm, and ventricular cleft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
